## Expired lease refuses renewal (red -> green, real PostgreSQL)

test=apps/dispatcher/test/integration/leases.integration.test.ts
      "refuses to renew an expired lease and keeps its generation fenced"
command:
  TEST_DATABASE_ADMIN_URL=postgres://moyu@127.0.0.1:55432/postgres \
    corepack pnpm --filter @moyu/dispatcher exec vitest run \
    test/integration/leases.integration.test.ts -t "refuses to renew an expired lease" --reporter=verbose

red before fix (base head 3278fb0):
  × refuses to renew an expired lease and keeps its generation fenced 23ms
    → expected true to be false // Object.is equality
  Tests 1 failed | 4 skipped (5)

green after fix:
  ✓ refuses to renew an expired lease and keeps its generation fenced 18ms
  Tests 1 passed | 4 skipped (5)

The test asserts: a live renewal succeeds; after `expires_at` is moved into the past,
`renewExecutionLease` returns false and leaves `expires_at` and `state='active'` untouched;
the same holder's `acquireExecutionLease` returns refused=stop_proof_required and the row's
expiry is still not extended. The fix adds `and expires_at > now()` only to the explicit
renewal statement; the maintenance queries in operations.ts keep their documented
"expiry alone never frees the slot" semantics.

## Verdict

Both stores were restarted (bridge 2107062 -> 2114387, dispatcher 2112165 -> 2114545);
ticket/assignment/admission/base/model/worktree and PG task/delivery/lease link are identical
field by field, the sync cursor advanced 100 -> 102 on post-restart traffic, and an expired
lease cannot be renewed or re-acquired without a stop proof. Item 4 accepted.
